<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sankore Madrasah</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sankore mosque-university, Sankore</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sankore Madrasah was an Islamic centre of learning based around the Sankore Mosque in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timbuktu">Timbuktu</a>. Together with other mosques and scholarly households in the city it formed a renowned network of teaching in theology, law, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonian-astronomy">astronomy</a> and other subjects. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai Empire</a> present it as a symbol of Timbuktu's flourishing scholarly culture under Songhai rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sankore-madrasah.jpg" alt="Sankore Madrasah" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anne and David · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2007_Sankore_Mosque_Timbuktu_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
